# Direct (first-order) dependencies of the Crypto Paper Bridge.
#
# Source of truth for *what* the bridge depends on. Transitive resolution,
# exact versions and artifact hashes live in `requirements.lock`, which is
# generated from this file and is the only thing the Linux installer installs.
#
# Relationship to `requirements.txt`:
#   `requirements.txt` is the untouched developer/Windows convenience list and
#   remains the file hashed by the TS-P0-001 runtime-baseline source scope
#   (`docs/RUNTIME_BASELINE_CONTRACT.md`). This `.in` file mirrors its direct
#   entries exactly; it does not replace it.
#
# `pytest` is intentionally retained so the locked Linux environment can run the
# exact-SHA Ubuntu staging matrix (canonical bridge item 9 / KVM2-P3-03) from the
# same hash-verified environment that will run the service.
#
# Regenerate the lock (network access to the package index only, no install):
#   uv pip compile IBKR_PAPER_BRIDGE/requirements.in \
#       --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 --python-platform linux \
#       --output-file IBKR_PAPER_BRIDGE/requirements.lock
#
# Any edit here REQUIRES regenerating `requirements.lock` and re-running the
# deployment tests; the installer refuses to install an unpinned or
# unhashed requirement.

